{"format":"hologram.registry.artifact/v1","id":"mcr.microsoft.com/cbl-mariner/base/core","fetched":"2026-09-25T12:12:10.642Z","source":{"name":"Microsoft Artifact Registry","api":"https://mcr.microsoft.com/api/v1/catalog/cbl-mariner/base/core/details?reg=mar","page":"https://mcr.microsoft.com/en-us/product/cbl-mariner/base/core/about"},"readme":"***Warning: Azure Linux 2.0 will reach its End of Life (EOL) on July 31st, 2025. After this date, it will no longer receive updates, security patches, or support, which could leave your systems vulnerable. We strongly recommend upgrading to an Azure Linux 3.0 image before July 31st, 2025.***\n\n## About\n\nThis repository contains the official base image for CBL-Mariner. Use Docker to run a standalone Linux container with core packages pre-installed or use it as a base for your own deployments.\n\n### What is CBL-Mariner?\n\nCBL-Mariner is an internal Linux distribution for Microsoft’s cloud infrastructure and edge products and services. CBL-Mariner is designed to provide a consistent platform for these devices and services and will enhance Microsoft’s ability to stay current on Linux updates.  \n\nTo learn more about CBL-Mariner, refer to our [GitHub repository](https://github.com/microsoft/azurelinux/).\n\n## Featured tags\n\n- `2.0`\n- `2.0-nonroot`\n\nThe featured tags are multi-architecture tags (i.e., `x86-64` and `aarch64`) that refer to the latest version of their corresponding images. Additional tags that are specific to Mariner build or architecture can be found in the Tags section.\n\n## Usage\n\nDepending on which CBL-Mariner version you want to use, replace `<tag>` with one from the Featured tags.\n\n    docker run -it mcr.microsoft.com/cbl-mariner/base/core:<tag>\n\nFor example,\n\n    docker run -it mcr.microsoft.com/cbl-mariner/base/core:2.0\n    docker run -it mcr.microsoft.com/cbl-mariner/base/core:2.0-nonroot\n\nThe default container startup command is `bash`.\n\n## Support\n\nCBL-Mariner container images are supported only for internal Microsoft use. For more information please see our [Support Statement](https://github.com/microsoft/azurelinux/blob/2.0/SUPPORT.md).\n\n## License\n\nThe CBL-Mariner distribution is provided under the [MIT license](https://github.com/microsoft/azurelinux/blob/2.0/LICENSE). Individual packages and components are governed by their own licenses included in the package sources available via srpm on [packages.microsoft.com](https://packages.microsoft.com/cbl-mariner/) or via our [GitHub repository](https://github.com/microsoft/azurelinux/).\n\n- Legal Notice: [Container License Information](https://aka.ms/mcr/osslegalnotice)","readmeBase":null,"publisher":{"name":"Microsoft","url":"https://mcr.microsoft.com/","official":true,"verified":true},"registered":null,"updated":"2026-07-21T16:58:46.6396558+00:00","categories":[],"keywords":[],"license":"MIT","links":[],"maintainers":[],"stats":{"pulls":null,"pullsText":"14.4M+","stars":null},"mediaTypes":[],"contentTypes":[],"storage":null,"tags":[{"name":"2.0","digest":"sha256:c833841d2dcfd3081d2ee807050d19368854f70d9b6faef027463e2c6f45ee41","pushed":"2026-03-12T21:00:45.0000000+00:00","size":null,"platforms":[],"mediaType":"application/vnd.docker.distribution.manifest.list.v2+json","status":null},{"name":"2.0.20260311-amd64","digest":"sha256:fdf30afe733831d3af0db95aa8e6870fb1094b2c4f531caaaa06e37481b95253","pushed":"2026-03-12T21:00:44.0000000+00:00","size":885,"platforms":["linux/amd64"],"mediaType":"application/vnd.docker.distribution.manifest.v2+json","status":null},{"name":"2.0-nonroot.20260311-arm64","digest":"sha256:4d7326523879f5e08d630998712b5931dd7ea869c4d21272ac653f62d74b6753","pushed":"2026-03-12T21:00:43.0000000+00:00","size":1632,"platforms":["linux/arm64"],"mediaType":"application/vnd.docker.distribution.manifest.v2+json","status":null},{"name":"2.0.20260311","digest":"sha256:c833841d2dcfd3081d2ee807050d19368854f70d9b6faef027463e2c6f45ee41","pushed":"2026-03-12T21:00:35.0000000+00:0